lifeos-nix patch f4-c — Ship PULSE.toml with the default-ACTIVE egress-capable modules off

PROBLEM
  RedTeam EGRESS gap (a): the shipped PULSE.toml sets three entries `enabled = true` that
  are default-ACTIVE (module loaded / job scheduled) rather than merely dispatch targets:
    - [voice]                     → VoiceServer module (cloud TTS path; already hard-killed
                                    by f4-b, but the module still starts by default)
    - [telegram]                  → Telegram bot module
    - [[job]] life-morning-brief  → 7am job, output=voice
  Every other external in the template is dispatch/target code that is env/cred-gated before
  the socket (verified: lib.ts dispatchSingle — telegram/email/ntfy all skip without their
  env var; airgradient-poll main() returns before fetch when AIRGRADIENT_TOKEN unset;
  work/calendar/github config-gated). Those are inert with no creds. The three ACTIVE ones
  are the gap: they load/run on a fresh install, so the point-1 invariant (default background
  egress ⊆ {Anthropic}) should not depend on "no cred happens to be set."

WHY THE FLIP SUFFICES (loader gates — pulse-unified.ts / pulse.ts)
  - voice:   started only `if (config.voice?.enabled !== false)`  → false ⇒ module never imported/started.
  - telegram:started only `if (config.telegram?.enabled)`         → false ⇒ module never imported/started.
  - job:     scheduler does `if (!job.enabled) continue`          → false ⇒ life-morning-brief never scheduled/run.
  The flag is load-bearing; enabled=false makes the egress code unreachable, not merely unused.

FIX
  Flip the three shipped defaults to `enabled = false`. This is the system-tier template;
  a user re-enables per-module via LIFEOS/USER/CONFIG/PULSE.user.toml (merged by name,
  user-tier wins) — so opt-in is one line, default is inert. observability/hooks/performance
  stay on (local-only: localhost:31337 dashboard + local processing).

SCOPE / CO-EXISTENCE
  One file, three one-line flips. Orthogonal to f4-a (lifeos.ts) and f4-b (voice/telegram/
  Doctor source). Complements f4-b: f4-b kills the ElevenLabs call in-code; f4-c stops the
  modules from being default-active at all.

VERIFICATION
  Hunks via `diff -u`; `patch -p1 --dry-run` clean; built PULSE.toml shows the three
  `enabled = false`. No behavioral egress reachable at idle with no creds.

